(D4: Discrepancy 4 - a failing `Write` never set the error flag, so a
 write failure was undetectable from Vox. LANGUAGE.md:3860 (0.4.7
 numbering) lists file operation failures as catchable.
 **RESOLVED - fixed by vox #48 (0.4.8).** Re-run against current main, all
 four failure modes now raise the flag and `On error` catches every one.
 The final line is the survival marker, not a verdict.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/D4.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   the write to an invalid descriptor set the error flag
   the write to a read-only handle set the error flag
   the open of an uncreatable path set the error flag
   the write to a failed handle set the error flag
   the write to a closed handle set the error flag
   survived all four failing writes
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called seedfile at "vf_scratch/files/lines.txt".
Write "alpha\nbeta\ngamma\n" to seedfile.
Close seedfile.
(1. a write to a descriptor that was never valid)
open a file for writing called bogus at 2147483647.
Write "one" to bogus.
On error print "the write to an invalid descriptor set the error flag".
(2. a write to a handle opened read-only)
open a file for reading called readonly at "vf_scratch/files/lines.txt".
Write "two" to readonly.
On error print "the write to a read-only handle set the error flag".
(3. a write to a handle whose open failed)
open a file for writing called denied at "vf_scratch/files/no-such-dir/x.txt".
On error print "the open of an uncreatable path set the error flag".
Write "three" to denied.
On error print "the write to a failed handle set the error flag".
(4. a write to a handle that was closed)
open a file for writing called 'the closed handle' at "vf_scratch/files/closed.txt".
Close 'the closed handle'.
Write "four" to 'the closed handle'.
On error print "the write to a closed handle set the error flag".
print "survived all four failing writes".
Close readonly.
